From c2af43501e28f58958cf2ee5d68a17bd5ac4c271 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:52:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Expose steering fields without silent request fallback

Replay baseline: r6x author head 7316c7f9fae1bc4a0b7ab1848de0db4143eec5d2 and preceding
0500-series downstream patches. The original base and validation entries
below are historical provenance; r6x qualification is recorded separately.

Base: complete r6v author stack and downstream steering through 0186.
Rationale: top-level steering fields were allowed as ignored extras, while
nested-only admission differed on nulls, representable zeros and strength.
Declare chat/completion fields and forward them through existing extra_args;
retain nested input compatibility and reject conflicting duplicate values,
unsupported request paths and beam search before dropping any selection.
Canonicalize scale once to FP32 after strict [0, 4] input validation, validate
named zero against the loaded capability, and report the failing parameter.
Quality: projection arithmetic, cache salt and worker state are unchanged;
strengths above one require the expanded GPU and serving qualification.
Validation: 79 CPU contracts passed, 23 CUDA checks skipped on CPU; GPU
fixtures now include scale four and actual chat/completion field forwarding.
Upstream status: independent downstream experiment; not submitted upstream.
